            "target_entity_type": "PhysicalScheme",
            "paragraph": "In this study, the SCS loss method was used for hydrologic abstractions. Originally developed for agricultural watersheds in the midwestern United States, the SCS loss method is an empirical relationship between the retention and runoff properties of the basin and the rainfall. This method combines all three abstractions (i.e., infiltration, land surface interception, and depression storage) into one term, the initial abstraction (USACE 1998). In this method, runoff depth is calculated based on the runoff curve number (CN) and total rainfall depth.",
